I could not read your current firestore.rules content directly (same binary/encoding issue as marketplace.ts), so please paste these in manually and adjust `isAdmin()` / `isSignedIn()` to match whatever helper functions your existing rules already define (based on your AuthContext, you're using a `role` field on the user's Firestore profile — reuse that same check here for consistency).

-----------------------------------------------------------

// Reports: students can create; only admins can read/update
match /reports/{reportId} {
  allow create: if isSignedIn() &&
                   request.resource.data.reporterId == request.auth.uid;
  allow read, update: if isAdmin();
  allow delete: if false; // keep an audit trail — never hard-delete reports
}

// Ratings: only the two participants of a transaction can rate each other;
// anyone signed in can read ratings (so ratings can display on profiles/listings)
match /ratings/{ratingId} {
  allow create: if isSignedIn() &&
                   request.resource.data.raterId == request.auth.uid;
  allow read: if isSignedIn();
  allow update, delete: if false; // ratings are immutable once submitted
}

-----------------------------------------------------------

If you don't already have isSignedIn()/isAdmin() helper functions defined at
the top of firestore.rules, add something like:

function isSignedIn() {
  return request.auth != null;
}

function isAdmin() {
  return isSignedIn() &&
    get(/databases/$(database)/documents/users/$(request.auth.uid)).data.role == "admin";
}

(This matches the role-based check your AuthContext already implies with
isAdmin / isModerator.)